{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And when the cloud lingered\"</b> — to say that if the cloud lingered over the Mishkan for many days, and that place was not good in their eyes, and they were very desirous and yearning to set out from the place, even so they would not transgress the will of HaShem. And this is the meaning of <b>\"Thus did the children of Israel: they guarded the charge of YHWH, and did not journey\"</b>, for out of fear of HaShem and their guarding the charge of His commandment they did not journey. And likewise if the cloud were there for a number of days, such as two or three days, and the people were very weary and their strength afflicted by the way, they would yet do the will of HaShem to go after the cloud. And He further recounted (Numbers 9:21) that there were times when they would stay only one night and journey in the morning, even though it was a great bother for them. And sometimes the cloud would remain by day and by night, for they had traveled all night and arrived at that place in the morning, and the cloud rested there all that day and all that night, and it lifted in the second morning and they journeyed. And this is a greater bother than the first, for the people would suppose that they would remain there and would unload the wagons and set down their burdens as is the custom of those arriving from the road, and when the cloud lifted they would have to reload and would not be able to properly prepare themselves for the journey. Or two days (Numbers 9:22) and they would journey at night. And it is possible that all of these befell them during the journeys that they made as recounted here, and not in some other manner, for the cloud remained from evening until morning, and by day and by night, and two days, and a month and a year. Therefore Scripture mentioned these specific durations in their detail, and there were years many as He mentioned at the beginning, as for example in Kadesh, of which He said: \"And you dwelt in Kadesh many days, according to the days that you dwelt\" (Deuteronomy 1:46)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:01.822079552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}